\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Israel  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  in focus as judicial reform plan hits shekel\b0\par\par\uc2 584 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2023\par 17:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates with late day recovery of shekel, \uc2 BofA\uc2  comment)\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Feb 22 (Reuters) - Israel's shekel was largely unchanged against the dollar late on Wednesday, recovering from further falls in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that some say could spark \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as investors fret over a plan to overhaul the country's judiciary.\par \par \uc2 The shekel stood at 3.633 per U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 1515 GMT, after softening more than 1.5% at one stage to 3.69, its lowest since March 2020 and after weakening 1.6% on Tuesday. One strategist at an Israeli bank said the afternoon bounce-back stemmed from exporters taking advantage of a higher dollar.\par \par \uc2 Since hitting a high of 3.34 on Jan. 25, the shekel has slid nearly 10% on talk of local firms pulling bank accounts from Israel and foreign investors staying away due to the government's proposed judicial changes.\par \par \uc2 BofA Securities\uc2  economist Zumrut Imamoglu said that while political noise does not usually impact Israeli assets or economic policy, "this time is different".\par \par \uc2 "If this sentiment continues, we expect further shekel depreciation. \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than increase its policy rate further, as it is close to ending its hiking cycle, and hikes usually have little effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the underlying factor behind depreciation is confidence," he wrote in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 The government's reform plan would give it greater sway on selecting judges, while limiting the Supreme Court's power to strike down legislation. New bills that received preliminary approval in parliament on Wednesday included one that would bar the Supreme Court from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in ministerial appointments.\par \par \uc2 "The weakening shekel trend will most likely continue as long as no reasonable compromise is reached," said Jonathan Katz, chief economist at Leader Capital Markets, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was possible to "smooth out sharp volatility", but was not a tool preferred by \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which declined to comment on Wednesday, has bought tens of billions of dollars over the past 15 years to prevent the shekel from strengthening too quickly and its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stand at $201 billion.\par \par \uc2 "If this (shekel depreciation) continues rapidly, we could see \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  hiking rates to 5% in the next rate decision (April 3), and possibly earlier," Katz said.\par \par \uc2 With Israel's annual inflation rate at a more than 14-year high of 5.4% in January, policymakers voted to raise the benchmark interest rate by 50 basis points on Monday to 4.25%, its eighth hike in a row. Yet, this was overshadowed by the judicial plan passing its initial vote.\par \par \uc2 Following Monday's parliamentary vote, \uc2 Citi\uc2  said it was going long dollar-shekel, targeting 3.95 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Critics say Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  - who is on trial on graft charges that he denies - is seeking legal changes that will hurt Israel's democratic checks and balances, enable corruption and bring diplomatic isolation.\par \par \uc2 Proponents say the changes are needed to curb what they deem an activist judiciary that interferes in politics.\par \par \uc2 Government bond prices fell as much as 0.7%, while the main Tel Aviv-125 share index dipped 0.5%, with both bonds and stocks also recovering from sharp early declines. (Reporting by Steven Scheer; editing by John Stonestreet, Alex Richardson, Sharon Singleton and Alexander Smith) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-2-22T17:07:07.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230222ej2m02303\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
