\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Israel  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  chief: No need to rush to raise rates while inflation contained\b0\par\par\uc2 784 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2021\par 16:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held short term rates Monday for 13th straight time\par \par \uc2 * Israel inflation rate at 2.3% in October, within 1-3% target\par \par \uc2 * Governor: Economy expected to grow at least 6% in 2021\par \par \uc2 * No plans to pre-announce \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  shekel at 26-year high versus dollar (Adds shekel reaction)\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Nov 23 (Reuters) - \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  is in no rush to raise interest rates as inflation remains under control, and will not pre-announce how much foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  it might buy to curb shekel appreciation, Governor \uc2 Amir Yaron\uc2  told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the bank held its benchmark interest rate at 0.1% for a 13th meeting, citing expectations inflation will ease in the coming year even as the economy rebounds from the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Inflation dipped to 2.3% in October from September's eight-year high of 2.5% despite bottlenecks and supply chain difficulties that are affecting Israel like other countries.\par \par \uc2 "We still have a very accommodative monetary policy," Yaron said in an interview, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had "more degrees of freedom" to maintain that stance as annual inflation is expected to stay within its 1-3% target range.\par \par \uc2 Describing inflation as an "inverted U", Yaron said economic conditions did not point to a sustained rise, so "we don't see a need to rush in anywhere in terms of our monetary action".\par \par \uc2 Analysts are split over when rates will rise, with some expecting a hike next year and others not until 2023.\par \par \uc2 Inflation, which only turned positive in March, has stabilised partly due to a stronger shekel, which makes imported goods cheaper. Yaron rejected the idea that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was allowing the shekel to appreciate to bring down inflation.\par \par \uc2 He said Israel was in a different position to countries like the Czech Republic which have already hiked rates, noting: "Their inflation is quite markedly ahead of their targets. And that is a significant difference from where we are."\par \par \uc2 ECONOMIC GROWTH\par \par \uc2 Israel reopened its economy in March after a world-leading vaccine rollout and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month estimated economic growth of 7% in 2021, although Yaron said it could be lower after a weaker third quarter.\par \par \uc2 "We haven't done the complete analysis but you're still in the 6%-plus," he said. "We are seeing lots of signs for a strong economy."\par \par \uc2 Growth should remain robust "as long as there are no variants completely resistant to vaccination".\par \par \uc2 The labour market remains a downside even though the broadest measure of unemployment has fallen to 7%, and Yaron called on the government to provide more training for people whose jobs have been lost to structural change.\par \par \uc2 Israel's economy has shifted over time from manufacturing to services, led by the booming technology sector.\par \par \uc2 "We're not trying to change the trend," Yaron said of the strong shekel. "We're trying to allow the economy to adjust to the changes."\par \par \uc2 He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally in markets to prevent big movements in the shekel, although there "there is no need to announce a specific figure".\par \par \uc2 "We are in what I would call back to a more discretionary approach," Yaron said, after the bank bought $30 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year under a plan outlined in January.\par \par \uc2 The shekel has been the best-performing emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the pandemic, having risen around 10% since 2020. It hit a 26-year high of 3.04 per dollar last week.\par \par \uc2 That reflects tech sector inflows, Israel's large current account surplus and stock market gains that have forced pension funds and other institutions to cap their \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposures, but has angered exporters. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/inflation-may-persuade-bank-israel-embrace-shekel-strength-2021-11-09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/inflation-may-persuade-bank-israel-embrace-shekel-strength-2021-11-09}}}\par \par \uc2 The shekel weakened to 3.13 per dollar from 3.11 after Yaron's comments.\par \par \uc2 Yaron said shekel gains were based on economic fundamentals but that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to ensure adjustments were gradual so that companies do not make "irreversible decisions just because of too sharp movements".\par \par \uc2 He welcomed the passing of a 2021-2022 budget this month, the first since 2019, saying it included long-due reforms and did not impose fiscal constraints. But the government must address a high structural deficit in 2023 and 2024.\par \par \uc2 Yaron said Israel's sovereign wealth fund should begin operating in 2022, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may make recommendations on inflation-targeting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/cenbank-israel-inflation-idUSL1N2OO0EL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.reuters.com/article/cenbank-israel-inflation-idUSL1N2OO0EL}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Steven Scheer; Editing by Catherine Evans) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-11-23T16:00:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020211123ehbn02p82\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
