\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Israel\uc2  seeks to prevent 'over-appreciation' of shekel -deputy governor\b0\par\par\uc2 550 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2021\par 14:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Jan 18 (Reuters) - \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to sharply raise its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is largely meant to help exporters survive until factors that boosted the shekel last year subside, deputy governor Andrew Abir said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it planned to buy $30 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2021 - up from $21 billion in 2020 and after the shekel, one of the world's strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hit a 24-year peak of 3.11 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 By Friday, the shekel had weakened to a rate of 3.28 but on Monday rebounded to 3.23 after a weekend where analysts questioned whether the policy would work to halt the shekel's gain of 10% versus the greenback since the start of 2020.\par \par \uc2 "We are trying to prevent an over-appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  (shekel) in the short term that will make it difficult for companies when the exchange rate comes back," Abir told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 He would not rule out buying more than $30 billion, saying: "If we need to do more we will evaluate it at the time."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said the shekel's strength partly stemmed from the dollar's weakness globally, but also from strong foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flows into Israel amid growth in the current account surplus, direct investments, large-scale foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales by institutional investors against their investment profits in capital markets abroad, and an increase in foreign investment in Israeli government bonds.\par \par \uc2 Abir said the rise in the current account surplus was due to a sharp contraction in imports due to the COVID-19 crisis and that decline is expected to reverse in the second half of 2021. At the same time, he said, it is unlikely that foreign equities would greatly outperform local assets this year.\par \par \uc2 "So part of those factors that were behind the strengthening of the shekel may not be as firm in 2021," he said.\par \par \uc2 Exporters have complained that the strong shekel makes it tough to compete.\par \par \uc2 "If these forces start to peter out in the second half of 2021 and the exchange rate has strengthened in the interim, it may be too late for certain companies that will have already made the decision to shift their activities abroad or close," Abir said, citing an already large spike in unemployment due to the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Since 2008, \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  has bought tens of billions of dollars of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to more than $173 billion. "We have enough reserves for a crisis. Now it's just a byproduct of monetary policy," Abir said.\par \par \uc2 He also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has moved into other monetary tools such as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buying bonds and giving low rate loans to banks to lend to small businesses since the impact from interest rate cuts - the key rate stands at 0.1% - is limited.\par \par \uc2 "All these things are there to help the economy get through this difficult time. So that when we come out of it, we'll be able to come out of it with a relatively strong economy that will grow stronger," Abir said.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Steven Scheer Editing by Mark Heinrich)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-1-21T13:21:56.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210118eh1i021j9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
