\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Strong Shekel Forced Record Levels of  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 (Bloomberg) -- \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $4.4 billion dollars in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during December, the most in one month since at least 2009, in a bid to slow the appreciation of the shekel.\par \par \uc2 Despite the outsized purchases, which brought total \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2020 to $21.2 billion, the shekel strengthened 7.5% last year against the dollar -- the sixth-most among a basket of 31 major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked by Bloomberg. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Amir Yaron\uc2  said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases will continue as necessary this year.\par \par \uc2 Key Insights\par \par \uc2 The fresh round of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases brought Israel\u8217\'20\'19s total reserves to a record $173.3 billion, or 43.3% of output, and Yaron has said the level of reserves won\u8217\'20\'19t limit the current policyIsrael\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen driven by factors including the current-account surplus and foreign investment in the tech sectorEarlier this week, the shekel reached a 24-year high against the dollar, as the outlook for economic growth in 2021 rises on the back of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s world-leading vaccination campaignMonetary policy officials have cautioned the strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could act as a drag on inflation and exports, but Yaron said this week that service exports have been notably good during the current crisis, and recently there has been a recovery in goods exports as wellMarket Reaction\par \par \uc2 The shekel was trading little changed Thursday afternoon in Tel Aviv , at about 3.18 per dollarGet More\par \par \uc2 For an explanation of the shekel\u8217\'20\'19s strengthening trend, and why \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  has had difficulty slowing its appreciation, check out this question-and-answer.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210107eh17007fm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
