\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  cenbank expands bond market  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , holds interest rates\b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2020\par 17:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds governor comments, market reaction)\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer and Ari Rabinovitch\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, July 6 (Reuters) - Bank of Israel Governor \uc2 Amir Yaron\uc2  said risks to the economy were rising due to a resurgence in COVID-19 cases, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  opted to focus on calming financial markets and ensuring the low cost of credit instead of lowering interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday as expected held its benchmark interest rate at 0.1% and forecast an economic contraction of 6% in 2020, compared with its previous view that the economy would shrink 4.5% this year.\par \par \uc2 "It appears that the health situation is becoming more severe," Yaron told a news conference. "The rise in morbidity data in Israel increases the uncertainty and is expected to delay the return to routine economic activity."\par \par \uc2 Still, with rates already near zero and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long-time reluctance to move to negative rates, Yaron said policymakers turned to other monetary tools. It plans to buy 15 billion shekels ($4.4 billion) of high-rated corporate bonds in the secondary market, and it renewed three-year low interest loans to banks to allow credit to flow to companies.\par \par \uc2 The move sent stock and bond prices higher.\par \par \uc2 He noted that the bank continues to buy government bonds and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Thirteen of 15 economists polled by Reuters believed the monetary policy committee would hold the line on rates after holding pat in May following a reduction from 0.25% on April 6. Two analysts expected a 10 basis point cut to 0%.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  economists forecast a recovery next year with growth of 7.5%, above its estimate in late May for 6.8% growth in 2021, although the jobless rate looks to reach 9% this year.\par \par \uc2 "The economy is not expected to return to full activity until the end of 2021," Yaron said, adding consumer demand is falling.\par \par \uc2 The bank's staff reiterated an estimate that it expects the key rate to be in a 0-0.1% range in a year's time.\par \par \uc2 After reopening the economy in May, Israel has seen a surge in coronavirus infections, prompting the government on Monday to re-impose some restrictions. ($1 = 3.4510 shekels) (Reporting by Steven Scheer and Ari Rabinovitch; Editing by Tova Cohen and Hugh Lawson) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-7-6T16:20:47.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200706eg7602iqq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
