\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Bank of Israel to hold key interest rate after April cut\b0\par\par\uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2020\par 13:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Rate decision due at 1300 GMT on Monday\par \par \uc2 * Rate lowered in April for first cut in five years\par \par \uc2 * Annual inflation at -0.6% in April, well below 1-3% target\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees 5.3% contraction in 2020 amid coronavirus\par \par \uc2 * reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/cb-polls?\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, May 21 (Reuters) - \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  is expected to leave short-term interest rates unchanged next week after a reduction last month aimed at helping the economy recover from the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 All 12 economists polled by Reuters believe the monetary policy committee (MPC) will keep its benchmark rate at 0.1% when the decision is announced on Monday at 4 p.m. (1300 GMT.\par \par \uc2 On April 6, the MPC lowered the rate from 0.25% for its first cut in five years, while also signalling a willingness to move to negative rates if the economy deteriorates much further.\par \par \uc2 Economists, though, believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will opt to keep rates positive for now, especially with the economy opening faster than expected six weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 "Negative rates will do more harm than good," said Ofer Klein, head of economics and research at Harel Insurance and Finance.\par \par \uc2 Instead, analysts believe, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stick to other policies such as \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy struggled under government restrictions that required most Israelis to stay at home, with the number of job seekers peaking above 1 million. Nearly 150,000 have returned to work and next week restaurants are slated to re-open, joining schools and shopping malls.\par \par \uc2 Of the 16,665 Israelis infected with the virus, most with mild symptoms, just 2,812 remain sick while 279 have died.\par \par \uc2 Israel's government has proposed a 100 billion-shekel ($28 billion) aid package to help the economy. Bank of Israel Governor \uc2 Amir Yaron\uc2  has supported the action, saying now is not the time to tighten spending.\par \par \uc2 For all of 2020, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecasts an economic contraction of 5.3%, rebounding to grow 8.7% next year. Its own economists project the interest rate will between 0% and 0.1% in 2020 and fall to 0-0.25% in 2021.\par \par \uc2 Israel's annual inflation rate fell to -0.6% in April from 0% in March, well below an official 1-3% target.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 3.5177 shekels) (Reporting by Steven Scheer, editing by Larry King)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-5-24T11:18:05.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200521eg5l01mpx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
