\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Bank of Israel holds key rate at 0.25%, cautions on coronavirus\b0\par\par\uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2020\par 16:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Key rate stays at 0.25% for 10th straight decision\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Minimal impact from coronavirus if contained\par \par \uc2 * Says will use accommodative tools if crisis persists\par \par \uc2 * Inflation slips to 0.3% rate in January, below 1-3% target\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says interim budget to hit growth in first half\par \par \uc2 * (Recasts, adds details, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments, shekel reaction)\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Feb 24 (Reuters) - \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  warned that the coronavirus could harm domestic economic growth if the outbreak was not contained soon, as THE policymakers left the benchmark interest rate unchanged at 0.25% for a 10th straight decision on Monday.\par \par \uc2 In its first comments on the coronavirus, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in its rate decision statement the outbreak was "casting uncertainty regarding future economic activity globally and in Israel, and regarding the impact on inflation and on the financial markets."\par \par \uc2 Still, it said it was widely believed globally that the spread of the virus will be halted in the coming months. In that case, "no significant macroeconomic impact is expected in Israel".\par \par \uc2 "If the crisis persists and spills over into additional countries, and particularly if strict preventative measures are required in Israel, it is expected to have a more significant impact," the bank said.\par \par \uc2 "In such a scenario, the monetary (policy) committee has a range of tools to make monetary policy more accommodative."\par \par \uc2 All 16 economists polled by Reuters had expected no change in the interest rate. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterated it will be necessary to leave the key rate at its current level for a "prolonged period or to reduce it" so that "inflation will stabilise around the midpoint of the target range ... ".\par \par \uc2 In a reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, it added that it was taking additional steps to make monetary policy "more accommodative".\par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have held firm in their view that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is the best way to prevent disinflation stemming from a strong shekel.\par \par \uc2 Since declaring it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily after its Nov. 25 rates decision, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought some $6.5 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the end of January. The shekel still appreciated 3% against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Israel's largest trading partners.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  noted this is a "development that continues to weigh on the return of inflation to the target range."\par \par \uc2 Israel's inflation rate slipped to 0.3% in January from 0.6% in December, well below the government's annual target of 1% to 3%. The bank said it was possible that the inflation rate would turn negative, but it is expected to move back toward the lower end of the target range in the second half of the year.\par \par \uc2 The shekel was steady versus the dollar at a 3.43 rate.\par \par \uc2 The bank remained upbeat on Israel's economy, which grew 3.5% in 2019, and said indicators from January pointed to further growth.\par \par \uc2 However, it expressed some worries over the year-long political stalemate, during which caretaker governments have been unable to tackle a rising budget deficit or pass a 2020 budget. A pro-rated version of the 2019 budget is being used until a government is formed after the March 2 election.\par \par \uc2 "The interim budget is expected to have a markedly contractionary effect in the first half of 2020," the bank said, "and there is continuing uncertainty regarding budgetary policy after the elections."\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Ari Rabinovitch; editing by Larry King) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-2-24T16:47:01.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200224eg2o02u8l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
