\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  to keep rates steady as  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  preferred\b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2020\par 15:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Rate decision due at 1400 GMT on Thursday\par \par \uc2 * Rate raised in November 2018, no changes at past eight meetings\par \par \uc2 * Annual inflation at 0.3% in November, well below 1-3% target\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $3.5 billion of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Nov. 25\par \par \uc2 * reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/cb-polls?RIC=ILINR%3DECI poll data\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Jan 8 (Reuters) - \uc2 Israel's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely hold the line on short- term interest rates for a ninth straight decision this week, after policymakers damped expectations of a near-term cut in favour of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 All 18 economists polled by Reuters said the monetary policy committee (MPC) would keep its benchmark interest rate at 0.25% when the decision is announced on Thursday at 4 p.m. (1400 GMT), despite inflation remaining near zero.\par \par \uc2 "Positive growth data and an improvement in the global environment will support the decision to leave the rate unchanged," said Alex Zabezhinsky, chief economist at the Meitav Dash brokerage, referring to an annualised 4% growth rate in the fourth quarter and 3.3% growth for all of 2019.\par \par \uc2 Most analysts had expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first rate reduction since 2015 at the previous decision on Nov. 25 but the MPC opted for no change and moments later, it began buying large amounts of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the shekel's gains.\par \par \uc2 Andrew Abir, a voting member of the monetary policy committee and head of \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2 's market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  department, told Reuters at the time that policymakers believed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was more suitable than rate cuts to lift inflation and boost Israel's economy.\par \par \uc2 Since the Nov. 25 decision, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought more than $3.5 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although dollar-shekel stands at an identical rate of 3.46.\par \par \uc2 "The bank ... will continue to signal that its next move is down," said Ofer Klein, head of economics and research at Harel Insurance and Finance, adding the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep buying dollars and cut rates in the first half of 2020 if necessary.\par \par \uc2 Citing solid economic growth, a tight labour market and inflation expected to move back to its annual 1-3% target in a year's time, four of five MPC members voted for steady rates on Nov. 25 although they held out the prospect of a cut should inflation stay low and the economy weaken, according to minutes of the discussion.\par \par \uc2 "For \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2 , inflation is not a trigger to lower interest rates," said Amir Kahanovich, chief economist for the Excellence Investment House. He said more likely, it will take either a drop in unemployment, a sudden market downturn or a sharp weakening of exports.\par \par \uc2 Along with the rates decision, \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  will issue its updated macroeconomic estimates.\par \par \uc2 In October, the bank's staff forecast 3% economic growth for 2020, an inflation rate of 1.2% and the key rate ending the year at between 0.1% and 0.25%. (Reporting by Steven Scheer; Editing by Toby Chopra)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-1-11T14:56:41.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200108eg1802u8l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
