\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  may resume  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 , Abir says\b0\par\par\uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 2019\par 11:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds Abir comment)\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Aug 13 (Reuters) - - \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  may resume \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the shekel's appreciation continues to push inflation lower, a senior official said in an interview published on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The shekel has gained nearly 7% versus the dollar this year. Manufacturers have called on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to restrain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , since a stronger shekel makes Israel's exports more expensive and competing imports cheaper.\par \par \uc2 Annual inflation eased to a 0.8% rate in June from 1.5% in May, below the government's 1% to 3% target range.\par \par \uc2 Andrew Abir, head of \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2 's Market \b \highlight22\uc2 Operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  department, said the bank is carrying out the same policy.\par \par \uc2 "If it seems that we are not meeting the inflation target -- one of the causes being the shekel's appreciation -- and if it seems the exchange rate is moving away from what it should be according to the fundamentals of the economy, then we will go back to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Abir told \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's TheMarker newspaper.\par \par \uc2 "The appreciation we have seen since the beginning of the year raises questions about our ability to meet the inflation target," he said.\par \par \uc2 Abir is the second voting member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy committee in a week to express concern over the shekel's strength.\par \par \uc2 "If we believe the shekel is out of the range we have in mind, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Moshe Hazan told Reuters. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on the table and if we see the shekel moving out of the range we have in mind we will definitely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Analysts are split over the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , questioning whether central banks can effectively fight the market. \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  has bought $90 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past 11 years.\par \par \uc2 Abir said the bank has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  significantly since January because inflation had moved back into the target range. He noted that it was tough to determine the correct level for the shekel.\par \par \uc2 "We do not want to change the exchange rate trend and create artificial depreciation -- but to make sure there is no significant deviation from the equilibrium, especially at a time when the inflation target is deviating," he said.\par \par \uc2 Abir said the bank has information on all transactions. "... We can identify transactions from accounts that operate according to algorithms and traders who are not interested in the state of the economy but work according to the momentum of the exchange rate," he said.\par \par \uc2 "If the exchange rate strengthens they think it will strengthen even further."\par \par \uc2 Israel's strong economy is one factor in the shekel's strength, but Bank of Israel Governor \uc2 Amir Yaron\uc2  said last month that interest rate increases were possible in the coming months, when other central banks were loosening policy. That led to a disconnect in what \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  was saying and what markets believed.\par \par \uc2 Yaron on July 31 backtracked and said there would be no rate increases for "an extended period", followed by a \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  rate cut. Still, the shekel has not weakened and stands at a 16-month high of 3.49 per dollar. It is also up more than 8 percent this year against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of main trading partners. (Reporting by Steven Scheer, editing by Larry King)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-8-16T09:54:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190813ef8d018zh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
