\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Bank of Israel holds key rate at 0.25 pct, sees gradual tightening\b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2019\par 17:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to add byline without change to text; recasts, adds governor's comments)\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer and Ari Rabinovitch\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Jan 7 (Reuters) - Bank of Israel Governor Amir Yaron said monetary tightening will be slow after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left short-term interest rates unchanged in Yaron's first decision.\par \par \uc2 All 10 economists polled by Reuters had expected no move.\par \par \uc2 Yaron was sworn in on Dec. 24 and replaces Karnit Flug, whose term ended in mid-November. At the subsequent meeting on Nov. 26, under deputy governor Nadine Baudot-Trajtenberg, policymakers raised the benchmark interest rate to 0.25 percent from 0.1 percent in a surprise move.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters after the decision to hold rates this time, Yaron said "the rising path of the interest rate in the future will be gradual and cautious".\par \par \uc2 Modi Shafrir, chief strategist at \uc2 Mizrahi-Tefahot Bank\uc2 's finance division, called both the statement and Yaron's comments "dovish".\par \par \uc2 In an updated forecast, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's own economists expect the key rate to remain on hold for the first half of 2019 and rise once in the third quarter to end the year at 0.50 percent. They foresee another hike in the first quarter of 2020 and a rate of 1.25 percent by the end of next year, with an inflation rate of 1.3 percent this year and 1.8 percent in 2020.\par \par \uc2 "If these forecasts are realised, they will be consistent with gradual contraction of the monetary policy accommodation," Yaron said.\par \par \uc2 In keeping rates steady, \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  said data showed the economy was performing well and the labour market was tight, with economic weakness in the second and third quarters due to one-time factors.\par \par \uc2 The bank believes continued wage increases will help push inflation higher.\par \par \uc2 Israel's economy grew an estimated 3.2 percent in 2018 -- below a 3.7 percent forecast -- and \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  expects a 3.4 percent rate this year, down from a previous estimate of 3.6 percent. It also set an economic growth forecast of 3.5 percent for 2020.\par \par \uc2 Yaron noted that along with a decline in Israel's current account surplus and the widening interest rate gap with the United States, the shekel has depreciated gradually. If the trend changes, that could slow the increase in inflation towards 2 percent, he said.\par \par \uc2 Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for almost a year, Yaron said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still one of the bank's policy tools.\par \par \uc2 "To the extent that there will be anomalous fluctuations that are not in line with fundamental economic conditions, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tool is still available to \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 The shekel has depreciated 2 percent versus the dollar the past six months. It weakened slightly to 3.70 to the dollar after the rates announcement.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Tova Cohen; Editing by Toby Chopra and Alison Williams) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-1-7T17:30:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190107ef1702o55\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
