\par\par \b \uc2 TABLE-Israel  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves rise in August to $116 bln, cbank bought $173 mln\b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2018\par 12:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Sept 6 (Reuters) - Israel's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves\par  rose by $223 million in August to $116 billion, its\par third monthly gain in a row and boosted by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  buying,\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Israel\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Thursday.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Israel\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has cut back on its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par market since purchasing $1.8 billion in January, sending\par reserves to a record high of $117.6 billion. It bought $173\par million last month, all of which were part of a programme aimed \par at offseting the effects of natural gas production on the\par exchange rate, after no purchases in July.\par     The August reserves total included $1.485 billion in special\par drawing rights from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par   \par                          \par                            (in millions of dollars)\par                          August 2018    July 2018   August 2017\par  Reserves                    116,005      115,782       111,020\par  Reserves bought under        12,923       12,750        11,540\par  natgas programme*                                 \par    * - cumulative since start of programme in May 2013\par     \par     -- Israel's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves represent 31.6 percent\par of GDP.\par     -- In addition to its own purchases, the bank attributed the\par rise in reserves last month to a revaluation that increased the\par reserves by about $262 million and private sector transfers of\par about $61 million. These were offset by government transfers to\par abroad totaling about $273 million.\par     -- In 2017, reserves grew by $14.6 billion. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of\par Israel\f28 \uc2 \f2  bought $1.5 billion of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as part of its\par natural gas programme.\par     \par     For full report click:\par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.boi.org.il/en/NewsAndPublications/PressReleases/Pages/6-9-18.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.boi.org.il/en/NewsAndPublications/PressReleases/Pages/6-9-18.aspx}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par \par  (Reporting by Steven Scheer; Editing by Tova Cohen)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-9-6T11:02:53.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180906ee9601frx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
