\par\par \b \uc2 TABLE-Israel  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves rise in June to $114.8 bln, cenbank bought $125 mln\b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2018\par 13:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     July 5 (Reuters) - Israel's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves\par  rose by $133 million in June to $114.8 billion, its\par first gain in five months, \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Israel\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Thursday.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Israel\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has cut back on its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par market, buying $125 million last month, all of it for the\par purchase programme intended to offset the effects of natural gas\par production on the exchange rate.\par     In January the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had purchased $1.8 billion,\par sending reserves to a record high of $117.6 billion. Since then,\par it has bought a total of $763 million.\par     The June reserves total included $1.492 billion in special\par drawing rights from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par   \par                          \par                            (in millions of dollars)\par                            June 2018     May 2018     June 2017\par  Reserves                    114,833      114,700       108,706\par  Reserves bought under        12,750       12,625        11,390\par  natgas programme*                                 \par    * - cumulative since start of programme in May 2013\par     \par     -- Israel's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves represent 31.8 percent\par of GDP.\par     -- The bank attributed the rise in reserves last month to \par its own purchases, government transfers from abroad totaling\par about $31 million and a revaluation that increased the reserves\par by about $6 million.\par     -- That was partly offset by $29 million in private sector\par transfers.\par     -- In 2017, reserves grew by $14.6 billion. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of\par Israel\f28 \uc2 \f2  bought $1.5 billion of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as part of its\par natural gas programme.\par     \par     For full report click:\par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.boi.org.il/en/NewsAndPublications/PressReleases/Pages/5-7-18.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.boi.org.il/en/NewsAndPublications/PressReleases/Pages/5-7-18.aspx}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par \par  (Reporting by Steven Scheer)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-7-5T12:25:41.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180705ee7500g4m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
