\par\par \b \uc2 TABLE-Israel  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves dip in May to $114.7 bln, cenbank bought $167 mln\b0\par\par\uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2018\par 12:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     June 7 (Reuters) - Israel's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves\par  fell by $654 million in May to $114.7 billion, its\par fourth straight monthly decline, \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Israel\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on\par Thursday.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Israel\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has cut back on its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par market, buying $167 million, mostly for the purchase programme\par intended to offset the effects of natural gas production on the\par exchange rate.\par     In January the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had purchased $1.8 billion,\par sending reserves to a record high of $117.6 billion. It bought\par $304 million in February, $143 million in March and another $24\par million in April.\par     The May reserves total included $1.461 billion in special\par drawing rights from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par   \par                          \par                            (in millions of dollars)\par                             May 2018   April 2018      May 2017\par  Reserves                    114,700      115,354       107,367\par  Reserves bought under        12,625       12,471        11,250\par  natgas programme*                                 \par    * - cumulative since start of programme in May 2013\par     \par     -- Israel's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves represent 31.8 percent\par of GDP.\par     -- The bank attributed the decline in reserves last month to\par government transfers to abroad totaling about $34 million and a\par revaluation that decreased the reserves by about $803 million.\par     -- That was partly offset by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  purchases by\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Israel\f28 \uc2 \f2  and $16 million in private sector transfers.\par     -- In 2017, reserves grew by $14.6 billion. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of\par Israel\f28 \uc2 \f2  bought $1.5 billion of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as part of its\par natural gas programme.\par     \par     For full report click:\par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.boi.org.il/en/NewsAndPublications/PressReleases/Pages/ForexreservesMay2018.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.boi.org.il/en/NewsAndPublications/PressReleases/Pages/ForexreservesMay2018.aspx}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par \par  (Reporting by Ari Rabinovitch; Editing by Tova Cohen)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-6-7T11:55:14.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180607ee6700ds7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
