\par\par \b \uc2 TABLE-Israel  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves dip in April to $115 bln, cenbank bought $24 mln\b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2018\par 13:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     May 7 (Reuters) - Israel's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves\par  fell by $773 million in March to $115.35 billion,\par its third straight monthly decline, \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Israel\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on\par Monday.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Israel\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has cut back on its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par market, buying $24 million, all of which were part of the\par purchase programme intended to offset the effects of natural gas\par production on the exchange rate.\par     In January the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had purchased of $1.8 billion,\par sending reserves to a record high of $117.6 billion. It bought\par $304 million in February and another $143 million in March.\par     The April reserves total included $1.482 billion in special\par drawing rights from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par   \par                          \par                            (in millions of dollars)\par                           April 2018   March 2018    April 2017\par  Reserves                    115,354      116,127       105,142\par  Reserves bought under        12,471       12,447        11,000\par  natgas programme*                                 \par    * - cumulative since start of programme in May 2013\par     \par     -- Israel's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves represent 32.9 percent\par of GDP.\par     -- The bank attributed the decline in reserves last month to\par government transfers to abroad totaling about $182 million,\par private sector transfers of about $37 million and a revaluation\par that decreased the reserves by about $578 million.\par     -- That was partly offset by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  purchases by\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Israel\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     -- In 2017, reserves grew by $14.6 billion. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of\par Israel\f28 \uc2 \f2  bought $1.5 billion of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as part of its\par natural gas programme.\par     \par     For full report click:\par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.boi.org.il/en/NewsAndPublications/PressReleases/Pages/7-5-18-Forex.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.boi.org.il/en/NewsAndPublications/PressReleases/Pages/7-5-18-\b  \highlight22Forex\b0 \highlight22 .aspx}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.boi.org.il/en/NewsAndPublications/PressReleases/Pages/9-4-18-Foreign.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.boi.org.il/en/NewsAndPublications/PressReleases/Pages/9-4-18-Foreign.aspx}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par \par  (Reporting by Steven Scheer)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-5-7T12:44:25.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180507ee5700ev3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
