\par\par \b \uc2 TABLE-Israel  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves slip in March to $116 bln, cenbank bought $143 mln\b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2018\par 14:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     April 9 (Reuters) - Israel's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves\par  fell by $313 million in March to $116 billion, \f28 \uc2 \f2 the\par Bank of Israel\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Monday.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Israel\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut back on its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par market, buying $143 million, all of which were part of the\par purchase programme intended to offset the effects of natural gas\par production on the exchange rate.\par     In January the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had purchased of $1.8 billion\par sending reserves to a record high of $117.6 billion. It bought\par $304 million in February.\par     The March reserves total included $1.518 billion in special\par drawing rights from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par   \par                          \par                            (in millions of dollars)\par                           March 2018     Feb 2018    March 2017\par  Reserves                    115,978      116,291       103,174\par  Reserves bought under        12,447       12,304        10,750\par  natgas programme*                                 \par    * - cumulative since start of programme in May 2013\par     \par     -- Israel's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves represent 33 percent\par of GDP.\par     -- The bank attributed the decline in reserves last month to\par government transfers to abroad totaling about $587 million and\par private sector transfers of about $6 million.\par     -- That was partly offset by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  purchases by\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Israel\f28 \uc2 \f2  totaling $143 million and a revaluation that\par increased the reserves by about $137 million.\par     -- In 2017, reserves grew by $14.6 billion. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of\par Israel\f28 \uc2 \f2  bought $1.5 billion of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as part of its\par natural gas programme.\par     \par     For full report click:\par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.boi.org.il/en/NewsAndPublications/PressReleases/Pages/9-4-18-Foreign.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.boi.org.il/en/NewsAndPublications/PressReleases/Pages/9-4-18-Foreign.aspx}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par \par  (Reporting by Ari Rabinovitch\par Editing by Steven Scheer)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-4-9T13:18:04.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180409ee4900gaw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
