\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Israel\uc2 : Computer driven trading is boosting shekel\b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2018\par 16:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Shekel up nearly 13 pct vs dollar since start of 2017\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fight shekel strength\par \par \uc2 * Foreign players boosting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade by 40 pct\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Bank of Israel\uc2  monitoring foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  conversion deals\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Jan 21 (Reuters) - \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  on Sunday said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading driven by computer models has jumped and is helping to keep the shekel overvalued, after it appreciated 11 percent against the dollar in 2017.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it has monitored every conversion transaction between Israeli and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as well as every deal involving the Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , index, and interest rate derivatives.\par \par \uc2 Israelis and foreigners who carry out a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivative transaction have been required to report such deals to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the past year.\par \par \uc2 "In the last month, we have seen a large increase in interest in the shekel by model-driven accounts. This would appear to have been one of the factors behind the shekel's appreciation," \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  told Reuters in an emailed statement.\par \par \uc2 The shekel rose to a 3-1/2 year high against the dollar in 2017, while it gained 5 percent versus a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Israel's main trading partners. In 2018, the shekel is up nearly 2 percent against the dollar to 3.41. Because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  thinks the gains are not necessarily down to economic issues, such as the current account surplus, it has been buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a more rapid appreciation, given that a strong shekel is harming exports.\par \par \uc2 "Notwithstanding the improvement in the state of the economy, which is a basic factor in the strengthening of the shekel, the shekel remains over-valued," \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 It said it "will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, as it has done recently, as long as there are exchange rate fluctuations that are not in line with economic fundamentals".\par \par \uc2 While in the past domestic banks dominated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, offshore players have now boosted activity by about 40 percent, the bank said.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Israel Governor, Karnit Flug, referred to speculators in a speech earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 "We have identified players that are not necessarily connected to real trading activity ... and we have also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in this regard," she said, adding that lingering expansionary monetary policies taken by some countries are also propping up the shekel. (Editing by Elaine Hardcastle) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-1-21T16:28:12.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180121ee1l00iip\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
