\par\par \b \uc2 Israel to let \uc2 Intel\uc2  pay Mobileye tax in dollars to avoid shekel rise\b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2017\par 12:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, May 16 (Reuters) - Israel sought to prevent the shekel rising further on Tuesday by agreeing to allow \uc2 Intel Corp\uc2  to pay the tax due on its planned purchase of Israeli autonomous vehicle technology firm Mobileye in dollars.\par \par \uc2 Intel\uc2  agreed to buy Mobileye for $15.3 billion in March in a deal which, if completed, is expected to result in a capital gains tax payment of $1 billion to $1.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 Israel had initially believed the money would fund tax cuts, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was worried converting such a large sum from dollars would further strengthen the shekel, which \uc2 Bank of Israel\uc2  officials have said is "over-valued".\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Israel Tax Authority\uc2 , accountant general and \uc2 Bank of Israel\uc2  said in Tuesday's joint statement that \uc2 Intel\uc2  will be able to pay the taxes derived from the Mobileye transaction in U.S. dollars "with the aim of preventing an impact on the exchange rate and over-appreciation of the shekel".\par \par \uc2 Any taxes paid from the deal could then either be deposited at \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  as \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves or spent abroad by Israel on arms or other items.\par \par \uc2 The shekel has gained 7 percent against the dollar so far in 2017 to a 27-month high of 3.6. It is also close to a 15-year peak versus the euro and at an all-time high against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tried to halt the appreciation through market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves hit a record high of $105.1 billion in April. (Reporting by Steven Scheer; editing by Alexander Smith) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-5-16T11:39:45.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170516ed5g00bt5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
