\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market to tame shekel rise\b0\par\par\uc2 187 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2017\par 14:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Feb 23 (Reuters) - \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  bought as much as $400 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, dealers said, as the shekel remained strong against the dollar and euro.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment, but dealers estimated the bank bought between $200 million and $400 million throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 After the purchases the shekel stood at 3.70 per dollar -- close to a two-year high -- compared with Wednesday's fixing of 3.71. Similarly, the shekel was hovering at a 15-year peak versus the euro at 3.91.\par \par \uc2 The bank on Wednesday said in a report it bought $2.6 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the second half 2016.\par \par \uc2 Its monetary policy committee "preferred to make use of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rather than a further reduction in the interest rate, because of the risks inherent in a negative interest rate policy," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in the report, reiterating that the strong shekel continues to weigh on exports. (Reporting by Steven Scheer, Editing by Ari Rabinovitch) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-2-23T14:23:09.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170223ed2n00fik\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
