\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  shekel weakens after  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2016\par 11:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought "hundreds of millions" of dollars of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  -sources\par \par \uc2 * Dollar-shekel had eased since Brexit vote\par \par \uc2 * Exchange rate stands at 3.8565\par \par \uc2 * Netanyahu economic advisor attacks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy -report\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold meeting with gov't officials on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comment)\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, July 4 (Reuters) - \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  bought "hundreds of millions" of dollars of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, dealers said, after the shekel strengthened for a fifth straight session.\par \par \uc2 One dealer at an Israeli bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started buying at a dollar-shekel rate of around 3.84. The exchange rate, which quickly moved to 3.85, had weakened to 3.90 on June 27 in the wake of the Brexit vote.\par \par \uc2 Dealers noted that some of the dollar gains after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had dissipated so the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  a second time. At 0925 GMT the shekel stood at 3.8570 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Its move came after financial newspaper TheMarker reported that the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy had come under fire by Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 's chief economics advisor, Avi Simhon, who was quoted as saying that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was tantamount to a protective tariff that raises prices for consumers by deterring import competition.\par \par \uc2 He argued, according to TheMarker, that only exporters are harmed by an appreciating shekel and they would be able to absorb a 10 percent appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for the prime minister's office could not immediately comment.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  has been buying dollars since 2008, boosting its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by some $70 billion to $96.5 billion. Its policy is aimed at protecting exports, which comprise about 31 percent of economic activity.\par \par \uc2 TheMarker said Bank of Israel Governor \uc2 Karnit Flug\uc2  had summoned Simhon and other government officials to discuss the possibility of an easing dollar purchases to weaken the shekel.\par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman confirmed there would be a meeting this month but downplayed its significance, saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "holds professional discussions on different topics with government officials from time to time" and this one will not be exceptional.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2 's position ... has not changed," the central said on Monday. "The hardship facing Israel's exports industries cannot be ignored, especially given its importance to growth and productivity in Israel."\par \par \uc2 Policy decisions, it added, are made by the four-member Monetary Policy Committee.\par \par \uc2 The dealer said it was likely \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease market concerns about a change of policy.\par \par \uc2 Flug told reporters last week that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was an "integral part of monetary policy" since it has prevented further appreciation. She noted that most central banks are adopting very accommodative policies that are acting to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "This situation may lead to an erosion of profitability among many businesses in Israel to an extent that will not allow them to survive this period," Flug said. (Reporting by Steven Scheer; Editing by Tova Cohen)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-7-7T09:29:56.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160704ec74002bh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
