\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2  shekel at two-month high;  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  seen  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 April 2015\par 15:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, April 29 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's shekel gained 0.6 percent against the dollar to reach a two-month high on Wednesday, prompting a third straight day of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said, bought an estimated $400 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the session as the dollar fell to about 3.85 shekels. It bought a reported $100 million the prior two days, after leaving short-term interest rates unchanged for a second straight month on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "The combination of the disappointment from \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2 's decision to maintain the interest rate unchanged - although the majority of the market was expecting this - as well as the euro-dollar strengthening to the 1.10 area, were among the major factors leading to the shekel's strengthening," said a dealer at an Israeli bank.\par \par \uc2 The shekel was fixed at 3.8720 to the dollar - its strongest level since Feb. 23, when \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  last lowered rates - from 3.8940 on Tuesday. It slipped 0.2 percent to 4.2624 euro .\par \par \uc2 When it last cut rates, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was to weaken the shekel and help Israel's export-dependent economy. That weakened dollar-shekel to as much as 4.05 from 3.86, but a lack of rate cuts the past two meetings has emboldened those bullish on the shekel.\par \par \uc2 HSBC\uc2  was not one of them. It had previously recommended clients take a position on the dollar-shekel at 3.99. But the position has closed after triggering stop-loss selling at 3.88.\par \par \uc2 Analysts believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep buying dollars to prevent a rapid shekel appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Over the first three months of 2015, \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  bought $1.84 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with $1.04 billion of that purchased as part of a programme to offset the effects of natural gas production on the exchange rate. (Reporting by Steven Scheer; Editing by Larry King) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-4-29T14:54:09.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150429eb4t00jot\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
