\par\par \b \uc2 Weaker Shekel Boosts Israel's Exports in March\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sara Thoth Stub   \par \uc2 184 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2015\par 12:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2    Special to DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JERUSALEM--Israel's exports grew for the third month in a row in March, mainly because of a weaker shekel, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Central Bureau of Statistics\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. But trade in the first quarter of this year was lower than in the same period of 2014, as weakness persists in global demand, especially in Europe, Israel's largest export market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Exports in March totaled $5.23 billion, up from $4.86 billion in February, the bureau said. The shekel has been pushed down by a stronger dollar globally, as well as by record low interest rates in \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's continuing market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including purchasing more than $3 billion in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2014.\par \par \uc2 For the first three months of 2015, exports were worth $14.8 billion, down from $15.8 billion in the first three months of 2014, the bureau said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Sara Toth Stub at realtimedesklondon@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 21, 2015 06:46 ET (10:46 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150421eb4l001x1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
