\par\par \b \uc2 Study Shows Companies Not Prepared For Employee Data Governance -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2014\par 12:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 6:00 a.m. EDT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Companies are collecting more data about employees than ever before, but most \uc2 HR\uc2  departments don't have the procedures in place to prevent the information from leaking or being hacked. In a new study by the research group Institute for Corporate Productivity, over half the respondents have no method for so-called "data governance"--rules and procedures for overseeing how employee data can be managed and accessed. (elizabeth.dwoskin@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @lizzadwoskin\par \par \uc2 0951 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] China, ever mindful of hot-money flows into its territory from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions, gave the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest moves a cool reception. "The EU is a major world economy that shoulders important responsibility promoting world economic recovery and growth. We hope the EU will adopt a responsible monetary policy and bear in mind the sustainable growth of the world economy so as to adopt a correct policy," China Foreign Ministry spokesman Qin Gang said. "When the EU was experiencing its debt crisis, other countries offered it support and assistance. We hope this kind of spirit of sharing can be carried on." The ECB on Thursday surprised markets with rate cuts and new stimulus efforts. (brittany.hite@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0944 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Indonesia's President-elect Joko Widodo said during his campaign that he would give greater emphasis to 'character building' than on sciences and more practical matters. But this prompted criticism that the country should instead be focusing on practical skills and science to boost labor productivity. Anies Baswedan, an education expert and a senior adviser to Widodo, says that Widodo's emphasis on character building did not mean to the exclusion of other needs. Indonesia ranks badly in \uc2 Transparency International\uc2 's Corruption Perception Index (114 out of 177), which is a product of education 2-3 decades ago, Baswedan argues. "I'm not putting my money into a company [whose integrity] is in question. Now imagine, if Indonesia is going to be part of the world and that aspect is not fixed, no way. So let's not say when you emphasize good character then you forget other things." andreasismar.sandiwan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0935 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Thursday's ECB easing pushed the German 2-year yield further into negative territory, resulting in the 2-year German/U.S. yield spread widening in the USD's favor to levels last seen some 14 years ago. \uc2 Barclays\uc2  says this spurred further EUR/USD weakness and looking at the charts, there is little support now ahead of the 2013 lows around 1.2750. EUR/USD currently trades at 1.2955. (gary.stride@dowjones.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0927 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  advices buying the dollar against the Israeli shekel, despite building expectations that \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Israel\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets. "\f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Israel\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's reaction function has clearly accelerated in terms of back-to-back rate cuts in the past few meetings. Given the extremely benign inflation outlook going forward, we do not discount the possibility of negative inflation prints and thus further monetary policy action by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Citi says. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  sees the BOI on a very preliminary stage at studying alternative easing measures. If the economy keeps printing lower inflation and growth figures the BOI may cut rates further, they say. (chiara.albanese@wsj.com @chiaraalbanese) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0925 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's plan to buy covered bonds as part of its asset-purchase program will push yields even lower, say credit strategists at \f28 \uc2 \f2 ING\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Yields are already wafer thin: on average, eurozone covered bonds yield 0.94%, a fresh low, according to Markit. While lower borrowing costs could encourage more issuance, a lack of mortgage assets and concerns about asset encumbrance may limit new deals, \f28 \uc2 \f2 ING\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. "The surprise decision to buy covered (bonds) is that it creates the opportunity for the peripheral banks to issue covered when retained collateral from the expiring LTRO is freed," they say. (ben.edwards@wsj.com @debtnerd) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0924 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Czech 2Q average real wage growth of 2.1%YY is small, but reflects the improving condition of the economy, says Michal Brozka, economist at Raiffeisenbank. Mr. Brozka expects wages to rise 1.7% for FY14 after adjusting for inflation, and then, as economic growth quickens, wage growth should accelerate to 3% next year. Rising wages will fuel inflation and eventually should allow the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to let the koruna float freely, but that's still in the future and today's data shouldn't dramatically influence the Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or monetary policy, he says. At 0912 GMT the koruna trades at 27.61 to the euro from 27.63 late Thursday. (sean.carney@wsj.com, @SeanCarneyWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0916 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Hong Kong equities end the week on a down note as enthusiasm surrounding a surprise rate cut from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peters out quickly in the city, even as shares in the Chinese mainland markets rally. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Seng\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index slips 0.2% to 25,240.15, closing the week up 2%, while H-shares move in step; the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hang Seng\f28 \uc2 \f2 China Enterprises\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index falls 0.2% to 11,368.34. Hong Kong's market "opened higher but consolidated afterward," despite the ECB's rate cut and strength in the A-share market, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 KGI Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 . China's railway operators erase most of their earlier gains after denying press rumors of an imminent merger, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 China CNR Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  (6199.HK) ending up 0.8% at HK$6.87 after retreating from a record high earlier in the session, and \f28 \uc2 \f2 CSR Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  (1766.HK) falling 0.6% to HK$7.10.(gregor.hunter@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @gregorhunter)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0913 GMT Eurozone money market rates, more specifically the Euro Overnight Index Average, or Eonia, will be more frequently in negative territory after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rate cut on Thursday, says KBC Bank analyst Piet Lammens. He now expects the Eonia fixing to range between -5 and +5 basis points. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0906 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] STOCK CALL: Shares of package delivery service Yamato Holdings (9064.TO) fell 2.8% to Y2,060 Friday following a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  MUFG price target cut to Y2,000 from Y2,050. The brokerage cited August 'takkyubin' data released after the Sept. 4 close showing handling volume down 3.8% on-year, well short of the company's goal. The results likely owe to deterioration in domestic business conditions and market share flowing to home delivery and trunk route operators, says a house analyst. MS MUFG keeps its underweight rating due to the firm's relative industry standing. (bradford.frischkorn@wsj.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0905 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Given that stagnation isn't good, some not so bad news from the second estimate for 2Q eurozone GDP. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Eurostat\f28 \uc2 \f2  confirmed that GDP was flat on quarter, up 0.7% on year. But consumer spending and exports picked up, and while the slide into stagnation was partly driven by a worrying decline in investment spending that suggests businesses were already spooked by the Ukraine crisis, a drop in inventories played a larger role. That's a residual, and you can never be sure, but with consumer spending picking up it may be that businesses got demand wrong and will quickly restock. There was also an unusually large, 1.8% decline in construction output that is unlikely to persist. It was bad, but it could have been worse. (paul.hannon@wsj.com. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @PaulHannon29) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0903 GMT The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's asset-purchase program will likely encourage investors to take more risks as they seek higher returns, say credit strategists at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2 . That could lead to complacency at a time when weak growth is rattling the riskiest corners of the credit market, they say. Last month, the bank's 'plunging bonds' index--a measure of junk bond prices that drop by 10 points or more--was the highest in 15 months. "Until the ECB's efforts are bearing clear fruit in terms of growth momentum in Europe, owning what you like rather than what you are forced to, becomes even more paramount in credit," they say. (ben.edwards@wsj.com @debtnerd) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 05, 2014 06:00 ET (10:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140905ea95000zv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
