\par\par \b \uc2 No Summer Lull for NY-Area Manufacturers -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,229 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2014\par 14:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 8:31 EDT - The \uc2 New York Fed\uc2  factory survey shows gains in business conditions, new orders and shipments for this month, putting numbers at multiyear highs. Employment also picks up. Fed inflation watchers will also notice the pickup in prices. The New York State report shows indexes covering both input prices and selling prices rising in July, although price pressures earlier in 2014 were higher. (kathleen.madigan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1226 GMT The Israeli shekel gains sharply against the dollar after the \uc2 Israeli government\uc2  overnight accepted a ceasefire proposal. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at its strongest level versus the EUR/USD basket since 2002, \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  says. "This market reaction is surprising to the extent that ILS did not come under any significant selling pressure through the past eight days of conflict \u8722\'22\'12 which we previously argued was consistent with the historical resilience of ILS to political risk," the strategists suggested. \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  highlighted \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's potential \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the greater risk for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (chiara.albanese@wsj.com @chiaraalbanese)\par \par \uc2 1226 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The Turkish lira has managed to fend off both the USD and EUR over the past couple of months despite a decline in the lira's carry advantage, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey\uc2  continues to ease policy. Economists at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  expect the CBT to deliver a further 75bps rate cut Wednesday and say that the accumulation of recent cuts, combined with inflation that continues to surprise on the upside may start to weigh on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leading them to stick with an overall bearish TRY view over coming months. USD/TRY now at 2.1210, EUR/TRY 2.8870. (gary.stride@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1208 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--Weaker inflows into euro-zone equities are likely to translate into a weaker euro, says Jens Nordvig at Nomura. "This is important, since strong portfolio flows have consistently supported the euro over the last 1-2 years," he says, adding that the ECB is clearly going to remain easy for very long. This is not reflected yet in rate differentials. "Hence, the euro's resilience in crosses has a lot to do with global rates still being under downward pressure," he says. (chiara.albanese@wsj.com; @chiaraalbanese)\par \par \uc2 1151 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--Credit market valuations are becoming less and less attractive for investors, says Giordano Lombardo, chief investment officer at Pioneer Investments. "Spread compression has continued across the whole ratings spectrum. The hunt for yield induced by central banks' zero interest rate policies has pushed the share of credit assets in household portfolios to unprecedented levels," he says. Meanwhile, liquidity in the trading market is fading. Even if investment-grade and high-yield credit retain some appeal in comparison with core government bonds, the upside potential is very limited. "Credit markets need to be handled carefully," he says. (chiara.albanese@wsj.com @chiaraalbanese)\par \par \uc2 1142 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--Gilts remain in the red after Tuesday's inflation data surprised to the upside (June CPI 1.9% y/y vs 1.6% expectations). This has pushed forward rate hike expectations, according to analysts at ING, who now see the first move in November. "This would also remove political concerns of waiting until early next year when election campaigning is in full swing and should keep sterling supported," says ING. The September gilt contract is 0.24 lower at 110.41 and the 10-year yields 2.631%. (nick.cawley@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1139 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Thailand isn't ready to raise rates, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says. "For the time being it is deemed appropriate for Thailand to adopt a relaxed monetary policy," \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  Gov. Prasarn Trairatvorakul says. "However, monetary policy may be adjusted...if the situation calls for it in the future." The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut its benchmark interest rate twice to 2% to shore up the economy since political unrest in November. (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1124 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] A bond backed by loans to Bulgaria's Corporate Commercial Bank, which last week had its banking licence revoked by the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has halved in price in the last month, according to a trader. The $150 million securitized bond--Northern Lights Bulgaria BV--which was arranged by Russian bank VTB is being quoted at a cash price of around 45%-55% of face value, the trader says. The bond had been quoted at a whisker below face value as recently as June 18. "Given the size of the deal and VTB as a sole lead manager, I don't imagine there is much of this trading or anyone who is willing to take the other side given a bank wind up in Bulgaria is relatively unprecedented," the trader says. (ben.edwards@wsj.com @debtnerd)\par \par \uc2 7:17 EDT - The only focus of the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this week's meeting will be attempting to fuel the country's tepid economic activity despite inflationary pressures, says Luciano Rostagno at \uc2 Mizuho Bank\uc2 . Like others, it expects interest rates standing pat as part of tomorrow's policy statement. Brazil's annual inflation in June surpassed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tolerance band of up to 6.5%, but some have predicted a below-zero number for 2Q GDP. (rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1108 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vows to maintain the stability of the Thai baht following calls from the military government to rein in the value of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "So far, the baht movement has not caused any problem to Thailand's trade or investment," says Prasarn Trairatvorakul, governor of the Bank of Thailand. "The BOT will stand ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the value of the baht weakens or strengthens too much and too fast in order to prevent any impact on local economy." Since the beginning of 2014, the baht has strengthened nearly 2% against the dollar, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 7:03 EDT - \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's (\uc2 JPM\uc2 ) bottom-line results haven't been impressive of late, in part on legal costs impacting earnings. That's kept shares going largely sideways the past year. The big bank's 2Q results are likely to please at least some with EPS falling much less than Wall Street anticipated as revenue dropped just 2%, not 8% as was the consensus view. "Core" loans rose 8% from a year earlier amid "record" business-banking loan originations while deposits climbed. CEO \uc2 Jamie Dimon\uc2  adds there were "encouraging signs" of increased business in numerous parts of \uc2 JPM\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the quarter came to a close. A real 2H economic pickup perhaps? Say it isn't so. Shares, down 1.9% since the 1Q report, rise 1.5% premarket to $57.13. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 1103 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] While the Aussie dollar is not having much luck on the topside, the U.K. clearer looks for buying interest in $0.9320 area to stem any further weakness. On the upside, the bank is looking for a return to the recent high of $0.9460 and on a break here, $0.9500. AUD now trades at $0.9374. (gary.stride@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 15, 2014 08:31 ET (12:31 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140715ea7f001sv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
