\par\par \b \uc2 Israeli shekel eases after finance ministry enters  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market\b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 2014\par 12:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Finance Ministry says hedging against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations\par \par \uc2 * Move sparks expectations for cbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Shekel has gained 10 since early 2013\par \par \uc2 * Exporters have called for weaker shekel\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, June 25 (Reuters) - The Israeli shekel eased on Wednesday after the finance ministry said it was hedging against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations, spurring market speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the shekel.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 3.442 per dollar by early afternoon, compared with a fixing of 3.433 on Tuesday, which was its strongest level since Aug. 1, 2011.\par \par \uc2 "If \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  it (dollar-shekel) could reach 3.40," said Rony Gitlin, head of spot trading at \uc2 Bank Leumi\uc2 . "\uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  but people are worried they might."\par \par \uc2 The shekel has gained 10 percent against the dollar since early 2013, hurting Israel's exports.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision on Monday to leave interest rates on hold, rather than cut them as a few in the market expected, has further supported the shekel.\par \par \uc2 After the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciated by 0.6 percent on Tuesday, the Finance Ministry said it had made two dollar-hedging transactions on its foreign debt worth $150 million to reduce its exposure to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate fluctuations.\par \par \uc2 "Market conditions, including the dollar-shekel exchange rate, support hedging transactions," the ministry said in a statement released on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The Finance Ministry has made a number of similar hedging deals in recent months. Finance Minister Yair Lapid has said he wants to see a weaker shekel.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the ministry's actions triggered some dollar buying by importers, who believe \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is independent from government.\par \par \uc2 Exporters have called for action to stem the shekel's strength, including setting a floor of 3.80 shekels to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  has so far rebuffed the calls for a floor, believing the exchange rate is stable after a steep appreciation in the first half of 2013.\par \par \uc2 Over the first five months of this year, it bought nearly $4 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although $1.5 billion of that was part of a programme intended to offset the effects of natural gas production that started in 2013 on the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  opted to leave its benchmark interest rate at 0.75 percent for a fourth straight month. (Reporting by Steven Scheer; Editing by Susan Fenton) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-6-25T11:50:10.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140625ea6p007py\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
