\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Israel\uc2  raises equity investment in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves\b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 17:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, March 30 (Reuters) - \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  said on Sunday it planned to increase to 8 percent its equity investment in the country's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in 2014, while starting investment in corporate bonds as part of a plan to allow for higher risk.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2013 increased its equity allocation to 6 percent from 3 percent and was expanded to Germany, France and the UK.\par \par \uc2 Israel's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves ended 2013 at $81.8 billion, a rise of $6 billion from 2012.\par \par \uc2 Some $3.2 billion of the purchases last year were within the framework of \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "intended to moderate exchange rate volatility which is not in line with fundamental economic conditions in Israel," it said.\par \par \uc2 Another $2.1 billion were purchased as part of a plan that began in May 2013 to moderate the effect of natural gas production on the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  noted that it changed its risk profile to allow for absorbing more loss without negatively impacting the achievement of the goals for which the reserves are held.\par \par \uc2 "The change in the risk profile was made possible by the increase in the level of the reserves and the integration of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases within the framework of the natural gas program, which are characterised by a longer term investment horizon," it said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aims to buy another $3.5 billion in 2014 as part of its natural gas offset programme.\par \par \uc2 Reserves reached a record $84 billion in February. (Reporting by Steven Scheer)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-4-2T15:09:18.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140330ea3u008kd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
