\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Israel Members See Stronger Shekel Threatening Exports\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sara Toth Stub   \par \uc2 424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 16:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  warned that a further appreciation of the shekel could slow a recovery in exports, a signal that it may once again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to the minutes of their late-February meeting released Monday, members of the Monetary Policy Committee agreed that at a time of sluggish world demand, the exchange rate threatens exports, a key driver of economic growth. At their meeting, MPC members agreed to cut the benchmark interest rate to 0.75% from 1.0%, the first reduction since September.\par \par \uc2 "Most Committee members agreed that if an additional appreciation occurs, it would be liable to undermine the recent trend of improvement in \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exports," the minutes said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets during January, buying a record $1.73 billion, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened 0.8% against the dollar during that month.\par \par \uc2 With the shekel hitting a fresh, 30-month high against the dollar on Friday, Israeli foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders say they expect further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in coming days.\par \par \uc2 "I wouldn't be surprised at all if we see another bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Eytan Admoni, manager of financial markets at Bank of Jerusalem. "I was astonished the bank didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when the shekel moves out of line with economic developments. Over the past year, factors pushing the shekel higher have included an increase in natural gas production, relatively strong economic growth, and interest rates that have been high relative to those of central banks in the U.S. and other large, developed economies.\par \par \uc2 To counter the specific impact on the shekel from higher gas production, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a program under which it will buy about $3.5 billion in 2014. But it can make additional purchases to control \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.\par \par \uc2 MPC members also cited slower inflation and rising unemployment as reasons for cutting the benchmark interest rate. They said signs of a cooling in the housing market opened the way for the cut, noting surveys that point to waning demand for home purchases and measures restricting mortgages as evidence of lower risk in the sector.\par \par \uc2 House prices have risen about 80% in Israel since 2007, prompting many economists and the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  to warn of a bubble in the market.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 10, 2014 11:27 ET (15:27 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140310ea3a0029c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
