\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Reserves Rise on Revaluation,  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Feb  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Waned\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sara Toth Stub   \par \uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 11:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM--\b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves grew by $811 million in February to total $83.98 billion, mainly due to an upward revaluation of the reserves as the dollar strengthened last month, \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  only bought about $350 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February, after a record purchase of $1.73 billion during January in an attempt to offset a strong shekel and protect the competitiveness of Israel's exports.\par \par \uc2 The bank said all of the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases in February were made under an ongoing program to buy dollars to mitigate the strengthening effects on the shekel of Israel's increased natural gas production. That program calls for the bank to buy about $3.5 billion during 2014. In addition to that program, the bank also has a policy to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, as it did very aggressively in January, when the shekel makes moves out of line with other economic or market conditions.\par \par \uc2 Partly due to the large purchases in January, and a decision at the end of February to lower the benchmark interest rate for the first time in several months by 25 basis points to 0.75%, the shekel was weaker against the dollar last month. But as many analysts predicted, the shekel has gained back some of that strength this week, as Israel's relatively higher interest rate and economic growth rate continue to make the shekel a safe haven for investors.\par \par \uc2 Write to Sara Toth Stub at realtimedesklondon@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 06, 2014 05:24 ET (10:24 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140306ea3600174\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
