\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Israel unexpectedly cuts interest rates to bolster growth\b0\par\par\uc2 791 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2014\par 18:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Cuts main rate by 25 bps to 0.75 pct\par \par \uc2 * First rate cut since September\par \par \uc2 * Cites weak consumer confidence, labour mkt (Adds shekel reaction, analysts' comments)\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Feb 24 (Reuters) - \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  unexpectedly cut its benchmark interest rate on Monday for the first time since September, citing concerns over slowing economic growth, although analysts do not expect any more easing.\par \par \uc2 A drop in inflation to 1.4 percent last month and a relatively stable shekel enabled the bank to resume an easing cycle that had been on hold for four months.\par \par \uc2 It cut its benchmark rate by 25 basis points to 0.75 percent, the lowest level since November 2009.\par \par \uc2 "Various indicators of activity in January pointed to some recovery, but consumer confidence indices continued to signal pessimism, and data continued to indicate a lack of growth in employment and wages in the business sector," \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  said in a statement accompanying the rate cut.\par \par \uc2 A relatively strong economy has helped Israel weather the recent turmoil in emerging markets reasonably well. Growth is projected at 3.3 percent in 2014 for a second straight year.\par \par \uc2 Still, data this month showed the economy grew by an annualised 2.3 percent in the fourth-quarter, well below expectations. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  noted on Monday that excluding the public sector, economic growth was just 1.6 percent in the last three months of 2013.\par \par \uc2 "This decision (to cut rates) will lead to a weaker shekel, which will help local industry improve its competitiveness and deal more successfully in international markets," said Zvi Oren, president of the Manufacturers' Association, who had lobbied the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hard to take action against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had appreciated by 12 percent since July 2012.\par \par \uc2 The shekel weakened to 3.5170 per dollar on Monday after the rate cut, from around 3.5060 just before the decision.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that even in the fourth quarter, a positive turnaround in exports was based mainly on pharmaceuticals exports which are generally volatile, while exports by labour-intensive industries were still virtually stagnant.\par \par \uc2 It continued to express concern about house prices though, noting they had risen by 8.1 percent in the past year while the number of transactions continued to rise and the volume of mortgages being granted remained high.\par \par \uc2 All 11 economists polled by Reuters had predicted no change in rates on Monday, citing the hot property market as a factor. Most believed the easing cycle that began in September 2011, when the key rate was 3.25 percent, was over barring a sharp downturn in growth.\par \par \uc2 SHEKEL EASES\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - which rarely keeps rates steady for more than four months - said in its statement that inflation expectations for the next year were well below 2 percent and global growth was weak.\par \par \uc2 "After two quarters of rapid growth, recent U.S. economic data were disappointing, though it is too early to determine if it is a temporary slowdown or a turning point downward. In Europe, slow growth continues, and there are growing concerns of deflation," it said.\par \par \uc2 At its last policy meeting a month ago, the monetary policy committee (MPC) voted 5-0 to leave the bank's key rate at 1.0 percent, citing a strong shekel as a key factor.\par \par \uc2 Since then the shekel has been relatively stable with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciated by 1 percent in terms of the nominal effective rate.\par \par \uc2 Ofer Klein, head of economics and research at Harel Insurance and Finance, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's arguments for cutting rates appeared similar to those it had used in recent months in choosing to leave rates unchanged.\par \par \uc2 "We believe the factors that tipped the balance towards lowering interest rates were weak data recently published in the United States and the possibility that the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also act to counter a continuing decline in inflation in the bloc," he said.\par \par \uc2 Even if the shekel - which is still near a 2-1/2 year high versus the dollar after a 9 percent gain in 2013 - appreciates further, \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  will use \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  over more rate cuts, he said.\par \par \uc2 In December and January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought more than $2.3 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a rapid shekel appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The MPC will revert to its normal six members starting next month following the cabinet's approval on Sunday of \uc2 Nadine Baudot-Trajtenberg\uc2  as deputy to Bank of Israel Governor Karnit Flug. She will start her new post on March 2. (Additional reporting by Tova Cohen; Editing by Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-2-27T17:51:12.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140224ea2o00cvx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
