\par\par \b \uc2 Shekel Weaker Against Dollar Following  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2014\par 11:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 xx-DJ The shekel continues to weaken against the dollar Tuesday morning as \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market after aggressively buying dollars Monday evening, according to Israeli \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders. The bank bought between $100 million and $150 million Tuesday after buying about $300 million Monday evening, following its announcement that the February interest rate would remain unchanged at 1%, traders said, although the bank declined to confirm the alleged purchases.\par \par \uc2 According to traders, the bank has already bought about $1 billion in January, about four times the average amount of its monthly purchases, and about one-fifth of its total foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases of $5 billion in 2013.\par \par \uc2 "Without the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we would not be trading at this level," said Tom Gerszbejn, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  / local market spot trader at Citi Israel in Tel Aviv. At 1001 GMT, USD/ILS was up 0.22% at 3.4966.\par \par \uc2 But traders said shekel weakness will prove temporary unless the bank continues to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively. Market fundamentals - including \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's relatively high interest rates, steady economic growth and shrinking government deficit - support a shekel that trades at least as low as ILS 3.48 against the dollar, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Israel's exporters, which make up a large portion of the economy, have called on the bank to lower interest rates and buy more dollars in order to prevent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength negatively impacting the competiveness of Israel's goods abroad.\par \par \uc2 (saratoth@gmail.com)\par \par \uc2 29 Jan 2014 07:55 EDT  Shekel Quickly Loses the \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Blues - -- Market Talk\par \par \uc2 1255 GMT 0000 GMT (Dow Joes) \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's widely suspected but officially unconfirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the shekel on Monday and Tuesday hasn't had much in the way of lasting effect. Indeed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already returned to the status quo ante and is above the level it hit prior to the BOI's move. Traders expected a bounceback given the modest, $400 million or so estimated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Indeed, Etyan Admoni, manager of financial markets at the Bank of Jerusalem derided it as 'peanuts.' The shekel remains in demand given Israel's strong fundamentals, however much local exporters might like a break. (saratoth@gmail.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 29, 2014 07:55 ET (12:55 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140128ea1s0013w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
