\par\par \b \uc2 Exports not that sensitive to exchange rate -Israel cbank chief\b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2014\par 16:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Jan 6 (Reuters) - Bank of Israel Governor Karnit Flug suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as long as the shekel's exchange rate was not acting in line with economic fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 The shekel last week forged a new 2-1/2-year high versus the dollar, leading to calls from exporters for more aggressive action from policymakers.\par \par \uc2 Exports, which accounted for a third of Israel's economic activity in 2013, are Israel's main economic driver and have struggled in recent years due to a weak global economy.\par \par \uc2 Flug, though, downplayed the impact of the shekel's strength on exports. She told parliament's finance committee on Monday that total exports were not "highly sensitive" to the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 A one percent appreciation leads to a 0.2 percent decline in exports, and vice versa, said Flug, who took over the reins at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November.\par \par \uc2 High-tech exports, which account for 44 percent of industrial exports, are least sensitive to the exchange rate. Still, the exchange rate affects the competitive ability of industries that compete with imports, Flug said.\par \par \uc2 The shekel appreciated some 8 percent versus the dollar in 2013 and its strength stems largely from Israel's economy growing faster than most other countries and the start of natural gas production, which boosted the current account balance.\par \par \uc2 To prevent a large appreciation of the shekel \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, she said.\par \par \uc2 "This \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is intended both to moderate sharp fluctuations in the exchange rate that are not in line with the fundamental economic conditions, and to offset the exchange rate's overshooting due to the effect of natural gas production," Flug said.\par \par \uc2 It bought $2.1 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2013 to offset the effect of natural gas output and plans to buy $3.5 billion more in 2014. It has also bought \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  outside of this programme.\par \par \uc2 "We are not indifferent to developments in the exchange rate," Flug said. "\uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2 's policy in this area is intended to make the adjustment period easier, and even to prevent excessive harm in the commercial sector as a result of the exchange rate overshooting."\par \par \uc2 Israel's economy grew an estimated 3.3 percent in 2013 and \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  sees a similar pace this year. (Reporting by Steven Scheer; editing by Mike Collett-White)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-CENTRALBANK/FLUG | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140106ea16000ph\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
