\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Israel\uc2  buys up to $500 mln of  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  but shekel gains vs dlr\b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Dezember 2013\par 16:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Dec 24 (Reuters) - Israel's shekel gained 0.4 percent to a nearly 2-1/2-year high against the dollar on Tuesday in the wake of \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  leaving short-term interest rates unchanged.\par \par \uc2 The shekel was fixed at 3.4880 per dollar - its strongest level since Aug. 3, 2011 - from a rate of 3.5030 on Monday. After the fix, the shekel gained further to 3.48.\par \par \uc2 Hoping to stem an appreciation that has reached more than 8 percent since early January, \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  bought between $300 million and $500 million of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout the session, according to dealers. \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 "What would have happened without \uc2 Bank of Israel\uc2  buying? Dollar-shekel would have been even lower," said one head dealer at a large Israeli bank.\par \par \uc2 With little foreign activity, most dollar selling came from local exporters, dealers noted.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  held its benchmark interest rate at 1 percent for a third straight month. Although analysts largely expected no move, dealers said some market players positioned for a rate cut.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come under pressure by exporters to act since a strong shekel makes Israeli exports less competitive. Since 2008, \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $50 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  although \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the shekel have been limited this year. (Reporting by Steven Scheer)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-SHEKEL/ | DA | ABN | M | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131224e9co000hq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
