\par\par \b \uc2 Israel should prepare for rate hikes as world economy improves-OECD\b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2013\par 18:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Dec 5 (Reuters) - \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  should prepare for interest rate increases once the global economy returns to normal, the Organisation of Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD) said.\par \par \uc2 Israel's benchmark interest rate has been lowered in the current easing cycle to 1 percent, with the most recent rate cut in September, from 3.25 percent to support economic growth.\par \par \uc2 "The authorities should set their sights on returning to more orthodox monetary and exchange-rate policy over the next couple of years if global monetary conditions return to normality," the OECD said in its 2013 report on Israel's economy obtained by Reuters on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "While monetary policy became even more accommodative in autumn 2013 ... a tightening phase will have to begin at some point," the report said.\par \par \uc2 The OECD also recommended the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "terminate systematic unannounced \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market".\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought some $50 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2008 to try and prevent the shekel from appreciating rapidly and further harming exports that comprise some 40 percent of economic activity.\par \par \uc2 It also is buying $2.1 billion of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2013 and $3.5 billion in 2014 as part of a programme intended to offset the effects of natural has production on the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also needs to take further measures to constrain high-risk mortgage lending amid a sharp rise in housing prices, the OECD said.\par \par \uc2 It urged the government to prioritise meeting budget deficit targets - unless economic growth falls substantially below expectations - to "avoid further deterioration in fiscal policy credibility."\par \par \uc2 Israel should be ready to raise tax revenues further, the OECD said, preferably by broadening the tax base and through reducing avoidance and erosion. Raising the value added tax (VAT) was preferable to higher income taxes.\par \par \uc2 An analyst at \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  told Reuters on Thursday he was satisfied with the recent improvement in government finances and said a sovereign credit upgrade is possible within two years if the trend continues.\par \par \uc2 The OECD projects Israel's economic growth at 3.7 percent this year and 3.4 percent in 2014. It noted that while Israel's growth has been impressive and unemployment is at a 30-year low, Israel must improve living standards and reduce poverty. (Reporting by Steven Scheer; Editing by Mark Heinrich)\par \par \uc2 OECD-ISRAEL/ | ABN | D | M | GFN | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131205e9c50010x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
