\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Israel rates to stay low while global policy expansionary -Flug\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Scheer   \par \uc2 485 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2013\par 16:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments)\par \par \uc2 EILAT, Israel, Nov 6 (Reuters) - Israeli interest rates will remain low as long as global rates stay at low levels, incoming Bank of Israel Governor Karnit Flug said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Flug has been acting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief since \uc2 Stanley Fischer\uc2  stepped down at the end of June. Under her leadership, she surprised markets by lowering Israel's benchmark rate by a quarter-point to 1 percent in late September. The bank held rates in its latest decision on Oct. 28.\par \par \uc2 "As long as monetary policy in developed countries, particularly the United States, is expansionary, our interest rates will also remain low," Flug said at an economic conference.\par \par \uc2 Flug, whose remarks were broadcast via video link, said very low inflation has made it possible for easy monetary policy but such rate levels encourage taking mortgages in the absence of other investments and lead to higher housing prices.\par \par \uc2 She said the low rate environment was one of the main short-term challenges for Israel's economy.\par \par \uc2 Israel's cabinet has already approved Flug for the post of Bank of Israel governor and she only needs the country's president to officially install her. That is expected next week.\par \par \uc2 Flug hinted that \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  would reduce the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the shekel from appreciating rapidly. A strong shekel harms exports, which account for 40 percent of economic activity.\par \par \uc2 She noted that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was just a temporary measure and exporters need to adapt and adjust to the reality.\par \par \uc2 "Ultimately, exporters will have to deal with the appreciation through productivity and efficiency," Flug said. "Once global economic conditions return to normal, there will be less than a need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Since 2008, \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought about $50 billion of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pushing its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to a record of near $80 billion.\par \par \uc2 Part of the dollar's recent strength stems from the start of natural gas production this year - meaning there is little need for gas imports and an improved balance of payments. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is separately buying dollars to offset the impact to the current account, after what Flug called an "over-reaction" by the market to the gas output.\par \par \uc2 "There are some who think there can be a strong economy and a weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but that probably won't happen," she said.\par \par \uc2 On fiscal policy, Flug said that taxes will have to rise as long as the government wants to spend on providing services similar to other Western countries and Israel continues to have a high defence burden.\par \par \uc2 She also said Israel could achieve both banking stability along with increased competition in the sector.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Ori Lewis; Editing by Jeremy Gaunt)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-CENTRABANK/FLUG (UPDATE 1) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131106e9b60012j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
