\par\par \b \uc2 Expect Monetary Policy Continuity from Israel -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2013\par 16:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 10:28 EDT - Israel appoints Karnit Flug to head up its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as Stanley Fischer's successor. But analysts don't expect any major shift in monetary policy. "This changes very little for the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, as Flug is considered to be Fischer's pupil," \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says. \uc2 Barclays\uc2  notes that \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  "has been slightly less inclined to use \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stave off ILS appreciation and more inclined to lower the base rate during Flug's term as acting governor." They expect "this dovish tendency" to continue with possibly one additional rate cut this quarter, which would bring the base rate down to 0.75% from 1.0% currently. (erin.mccarthy@wsj.com; @eemccarthy)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2181 or john.shipman@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 1427 GMT Monday sees low turnover and a very slight steepening of the curve, with investors sidelined - awaiting Tuesday's primary market bond tender. "Tomorrow's auction will show true appetite for Polish paper," the dealer says, adding market sentiment is rather positive, with the outlook for the U.S. Fed tapering pushed back until March. Poland will offer PLN 8B-PLN 12B ($2.61B-$3.92B) in various maturities Tuesday. Today, average yield on two-year paper is down to 3.06% from 3.09% late Friday, yield on five-year bond is up to 3.56% from 3.50% and yield on 10-year is at 4.27% from 4.23%.(patryk.wasilewski@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1410 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Intesa Sanpaolo\uc2  thinks it is advisable to avoid Italian (BTP) vs. Spanish (Bono) bond spread positions, arguing that Italy and Spain share "very similar" risk factors, and must still overcome numerous obstacles along their respective normalisation path. Strategist Chiara Manenti says such spread positions are exposed to event volatility: she thus prefers outright positions, aimed at maximising carry on the different segments of the two curves. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 10:10 EDT - The annual rate of existing-home sales fell in September and August's figure was revised lower, all suggesting higher mortgage rates are cutting into activity--but not enough to derail housing's recovery. With borrowing rates back in a range that's still historically low, more buyers are likely to trickle back into the market near-term. As long as job markets hold up. (kathleen.madigan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1237 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD's 2013 peak near 1.3710 may hold on initial attempts says \uc2 Barclays\uc2 , but the bank is looking to buy any dips into the 1.3645-1.3610 area for an eventual topside breach. This would then have a target of the trendline near 1.3990. The bank has read the market well so far: Friday's peak was a fresh 8 1/2-month high of 1.3704, Monday's range has been 1.3690-1.3664, with the low just seen. -- (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0000 GMT (Dow Jones)--\par \par \uc2 Tuesday, October 22\par \par \uc2 0830 GMT Spain: EUR 2.5B-EUR 3.5B 3-month, 9-month T-bills\par \par \uc2 0900 GMT Switzerland: 91-day T-bills (open volume)\par \par \uc2 0930 GMT Hungary: HUF 40B 3-month T-bills\par \par \uc2 0930 GMT Poland: PLN 8B-PLN 12B January 2016 zero coupon note, 2.75% August 2023 inflation-indexed bond, 4.00% October 2023\par \par \uc2 1030 GMT ESM: up to EUR 2.5B 6-month bills\par \par \uc2 Wednesday, October 23\par \par \uc2 0930 GMT Germany: EUR 2B 2.50% July 2044 Bund\par \par \uc2 1000 GMT Czech: CZK 2B-CZK 5B 0.50% July 2016, CZK 2B-CZK 5B 1.50% October 2019\par \par \uc2 After 1530 GMT Italy: Details of CTZ/BTPei auction on Oct. 28\par \par \uc2 Thursday, October 24\par \par \uc2 0930 GMT Hungary: HUF 40B 12-month T-bills\par \par \uc2 1200 GMT Hungary: target volume for 3-month T-bill auction on Oct. 29\par \par \uc2 After 1530 GMT Italy: target volume for 12-month T-bill auction on Oct. 29\par \par \uc2 Friday, October 25\par \par \uc2 0900 GMT France: details of T-bill auction on Oct. 28\par \par \uc2 1000 GMT Belgium: 2nd announcement (target volume) of bond auction on Oct. 28\par \par \uc2 After 1530 GMT Italy: details of BTP auction on Oct. 30\par \par \uc2 Xxxx Weekly EMU bond supply preview\par \par \uc2 (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1208 GMT [Dow Jones]--There are signs of life in USD/JPY, but only just. The spot clears offers reported around 98.10 to print a fresh day high of 98.18. There is talk of stops up at 98.30, and the 50-day moving average resistance comes in at 98.40. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1206 GMT [Dow Jones]--It's rates decision week for both Sweden and Norway, and both are expected to stand pat on rates at 1.5% and 1% respectively when they meet on Thursday. \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  says the drop back in inflation implies little change in stance from the \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2 . But with Norwegian policy rates still likely to rise before those in Sweden, the bank's bias is for NOK/SEK to move higher. NOK/SEK is now at 1.0866, from the 9-year low of 1.0578 seen at the start of October. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 7:57 EDT - \uc2 Barclays\uc2  expects a September nonfarm payrolls gain of 200k (vs consensus 180k) and unemployment rate to drop to 7.2% from 7.3%. In addition, fallout from the government shutdown/debt ceiling fight "is likely to be limited, and should not be the driving factor behind Fed policy," firm says. With that in mind, \uc2 Barclays\uc2  thinks December "remains the most likely timing for tapering, given our forecast of a pickup in payroll growth in Q4 over Q3." While some data collection has been missed during the shutdown, "the most important indicators, such as the labor market report for October, will be available," the firm adds. (john.shipman@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (212) 416-2181 or john.shipman@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 1139 GMT [Dow Jones]--The fact AUD's recent independent strength has been a function of receding RBA rate cut and improved China growth expectations means this week is an important one for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's near-term direction, says \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 . Wednesday sees the release of Australian CPI, while Thursday sees China's flash PMI. For the former, RBC expects underlying inflationary pressures to remain muted, with a +0.6% Q-Q print, which should reinforce the RBA's view that an easing bias remains appropriate. For the latter, RBC says the consensus is for a reading of 50.4 from last month's weaker-than-expected final PMI of 50.2 (flash 51.2). AUD/USD now at 0.9680. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1119 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore shares end nearly flat Monday on a lack of trading cues. The STI closes 0.09% or 2.86 points higher at 3195.70. Gainers outweigh losers 314 to 126. A total of 4.3 billion shares change hands at a value of S$1.3 billion, more than twice Friday's volume of 1.7 billion shares. Shares of \uc2 LionGold Corp\uc2 . (A78.SG), \uc2 Asiasons Capital Ltd\uc2 . (5ET.SG) and \uc2 Blumont Group Ltd\uc2 . (A33.SG) soar after the \uc2 Singapore Exchange\uc2  lifts trading restrictions. LionGold gains 90% to S$0.29, while Blumont gains 80% and closes at S$0.24. Among large-cap stocks, \uc2 Genting Singapore Plc\uc2  (G13.SG) closes 1.7% higher at S$1.21 per share, while \uc2 Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp\uc2 . (O39.SG) closes at S$8.35, down 0.9%. (jake.watts@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1117 GMT [Dow Jones] Euro Overnight Index Average fixed higher Friday at 0.093% versus Thursday's 0.088%. Monday, the interbank overnight rate is trading in a narrower range between positive 0.05% and 0.11% versus negative 0.02% and positive 0.13% Friday. Volumes are rather low, says a trader. "There has been barely any demand for the [ECB's] marginal lending for a week, which indicates that the market is calm," she notes. Earlier Monday, 3-month Euribor fixed at 0.223% versus 0.224% Friday. (friedrich.geiger@wsj.com) Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 21, 2013 10:28 ET (14:28 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131021e9al00336\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
