\par\par \b \uc2 Change of Guard at Israel's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 , But Policy Path Intact -- WSJ Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2013\par 18:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (This story has been posted on The Wall Street Journal Online's Middle East Real Time blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/middleeast/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/middleeast/}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 By Joshua Mitnick\par \par \uc2 Despite the swirling speculation towards the end of Israel's tortured four-month search for a successor to Stanley Fischer, the appointment of Karnit Flug as Bank of Israel Governor -- the first woman to get the job -- failed to stir up much excitement amongst investors and analysts.\par \par \uc2 That's because Ms. Flug, for the foreseeable future anyway, is seen continuing with the monetary policies of her predecessor. And that means keeping interest rates relaxed enough to spur economic growth and making modest \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong shekel and keep the country's exporters competitive.\par \par \uc2 "More than anyone else there shouldn't be any surprise," said Jonathan Katz, an economist at HSBC Israel. "We know that her world view is rather similar to Stanley Fischer's."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appointment certainly had little impact on financial markets. The Tel Aviv Stock Exchange's benchmark TA-25 Index rose just 0.7 percent in the hours after the announcement.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps Ms. Flug's biggest hurdle will be living up to the outsized reputation of Mr. Fischer's tenure. The former bank of Israel governor won high praise for guiding the country's economy through the fallout from the 2008 financial meltdown with few scratches. Ms. Flug can expect constant comparisons to her predecessor.\par \par \uc2 Beyond that, her main policy challenge will be balancing the need to keep the shekel weak to help Israel's export dependent economy, while avoiding the creation of bubbles in the local housing and stock markets, say analysts. Of particular concern are surging real estate prices, though that problem is seen as a result of tight supply, say analysts, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has few tools in its box to reverse the trend.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps Ms. Flug's first real challenge will come when it's time to raise interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "With all the noise around the process of the appointment, it isn't a critical factor for the capital markets," said Alex Zabezhinsky, chief economist at Meitav DS Securities. "She will be judged when policy needs to be changed -- whether it is done too soon or too late. That won't happen soon." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 . \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 20, 2013 12:31 ET (16:31 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131020e9ak0001s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
