\par\par \b \uc2 PREVIEW-Bank of Israel seen holding rates for 4th straight month\b0\par\par\uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2013\par 13:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Shekel at more than 2-year peak vs dollar\par \par \uc2 * Economy grew annualised 4.9 pct in Q2\par \par \uc2 * Rates decision expected Monday at 1200 GMT\par \par \uc2 By Steven Scheer\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Sept 22 (Reuters) - \uc2 Israel's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to leave short-term interest rates unchanged for a fourth straight month due to moderate economic growth and continued gains in home prices.\par \par \uc2 Along with a tame annual inflation rate of 1.3 percent, the most compelling reason to ease policy again would be a more than two-year peak of the shekel against the dollar at a level of 3.50. But analysts believe \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  has other tools - such as market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - it is more likely to use to try to prevent a further appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That is because the benchmark interest rate is already at 1.25 percent and a quarter-point reduction would likely have minimal impact on the shekel or the economy, they say.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2 's monetary policy committee has been led by deputy governor Karnit Flug since July, after \uc2 Stanley Fischer\uc2  stepped down at the end of June. Naming a replacement has hit a number of snags but the government is expected to announce a new governor in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  is slated to announce its rates decision for October on Monday at 3 pm (1200 GMT). It last lowered rates in May, by a total of 50 basis points in two reductions.\par \par \uc2 "The loose monetary stance that has been in place since the third quarter of 2012 remains intact but further easing is becoming unlikely," said Tevfik Aksoy, an emerging markets economist at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The main issue (for \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2 ) is the appreciation pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said, adding the shekel should stay strong due to a sound economy and natural gas output boosting Israel's current account surplus.\par \par \uc2 Much of the shekel's recent gains have also come as U.S. military action in Syria has become unlikely, while the Federal Reserve has delayed tapering off its U.S. bond buying programme - a combination that lifted most global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Helped by the start of natural gas production at the end of March and robust consumer and state spending, the economy is likely headed for growth of at least 3.4 percent in 2013, according to estimates from the government and analysts. The economy grew an annualised 4.9 percent in the second quarter.\par \par \uc2 Along with the rates decision, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's research staff on Monday are also expected to publish revisions to their economic growth estimates. \uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2 's economists currently project a 2013 growth rate of 3.8 percent, including a 1 percentage point contribution from natural gas, and a 3.3 percent pace in 2014.\par \par \uc2 "With growth remaining reasonably resilient and home prices rising, we think \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  is reluctant to cut further," said Daniel Hewitt, an emerging markets economist at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 . "With the housing market heating up, \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  wants to avoid sparking a bubble."\par \par \uc2 Partly due to low interest rates, home prices have jumped more than 50 percent in recent years, leading the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to place restrictions on mortgages. But those steps have not worked since demand has outstripped supply, while real estate has proven to be among the best investments of late.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Pravin Char)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-RATES/ (PREVIEW) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | GFN | GBN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130925e99m000hb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
