\par\par \b \uc2 Israeli shekel slides, stocks fall on talk of attack on Syria\b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Scheer   \par \uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 2013\par 16:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM, Aug 27 (Reuters) - Growing speculation about Western military action against neighbouring Syria weakened the shekel and Israeli share prices on Tuesday, sending the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a six-week low against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The shekel had been one of the best-performing emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year but it has shed almost half its 2013 gains on fears of Western military action in Syria that could lead to a wider conflict in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 The shekel was fixed at 3.657 per dollar, its weakest level since July 8 and a 1.5 percent drop from 3.603 on Monday. In two sessions, the shekel has lost some 2 percent.\par \par \uc2 "It is purely Syria on how it affects Israel but also how it affects the world," said Rony Gitlin, head of spot trading at Bank Leumi, adding that dollar buying was mainly by foreign banks that were also selling other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The United States has called for accountability for those responsible for a gas attack in Syria last week that killed hundreds of civilians, and calls for retribution have come also from some of its allies despite Russian and Chinese opposition.\par \par \uc2 Talk of Western military action has fuelled a sell-off in other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the lira in Turkey - another of Syria's neighbours - hitting a record low , and Russia's rouble at its weakest in four years against a dollar-euro basket\par \par \uc2 Should there be no attack, Gitlin said the shekel - boosted this year by steady economic growth and the start to natural gas production - would resume its appreciation trend.\par \par \uc2 A strong shekel had been a particular concern for policymakers since a robust \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  harms exports, which account for some 40 percent of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic activity. In addition to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  from time to time in the market, \uc2 the Bank of Israel\uc2  lowered its benchmark interest rate twice in May, citing a strong shekel that neared a two-year peak.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stability of late was one reason the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cited for leaving rates on hold on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Daniel Rapoport, head of equities and derivatives trading at Leumi Capital Markets, said the threat of a wider conflict led to across-the-board selling of stocks in Tel Aviv and redemptions by mutual funds.\par \par \uc2 In late trading, the blue-chip Tel Aviv 25 index was down 2.0 percent at 1161.02 points, while the broader TA-100 index was 1.8 percent lower at 1063.14. Volume of 1.4 billion shekels ($384 million) was above average.\par \par \uc2 "People fear that this could escalate and Israel would be attacked after Syria is attacked," Rapoport said.\par \par \uc2 Government bond prices fell as much as 0.3 percent.   (Reporting by Steven Scheer; editing by Stephen Nisbet)\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL-MARKETS/SYRIA | ABN | D | E | RBN | GFN | M | GBN | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130827e98r000ny\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
