\par\par \b \uc2 Revaluation, Market  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Boosts  \highlight22\uc2 Israel \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Reserves\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sara Toth Stub   \par \uc2 159 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2013\par 10:58\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Special to DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 JERUSALEM--\uc2 The Bank of Israel\uc2  said Wednesday its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves increased last month, boosted by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and an upward revaluation of reserves.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $79.1 billion at the end of July, up from $78.2 billion at the end of June. The bank said it bought $225 million in July under a program announced in May to purchase $2 billion annually on the open market to offset the strengthening shekel.\par \par \uc2 Iraeli natural gas production, which began in March, has boosted the shekel as it reduces Israel's need for dollars to buy foreign energy. A stronger shekel could make Israel's exports-- a cornerstone of its economy-- less competitive abroad, so the bank maintains a policy of market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Write to Sara Toth Stub at realtimedesklondon@dowjones.com [ 07-08-13 0858GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020130807e9870000d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
